LFD fills at low level now produce 1 tank, 1 healer, 3 dps.

Touches: modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/Factory/AiFactory.cpp
         (AiFactory::GetPlayerSpecTab untalented defaults),
         modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
         (FillLfgRaidGroup counts declared roles)

Why: report #129 -- "no more xml errors in the group finder, but it's also
giving me groups with 1 tank and 4 dps, 5 dps, etc instead of 1 tank, 1
healer, 3 dps". Reported the day the Classic/BC dungeon queues shipped
(rev_lfg_legacy_queues.sql), and the failure is specific to the LOW level
bands those queues opened.

Two compounding causes, both role-resolution:

  1. AiFactory::GetPlayerSpecTab's fallback for a bot with no talent points
     (below level 10, or freshly created) handed every role-capable class a
     DPS tab by default: arms warrior, ret paladin, balance druid, enhance
     shaman. PlayerbotAI::GetDungeonRole reads that same tab, so every
     untalented bot in the band both PLAYED and COUNTED as dps. The band
     literally contained no tank or healer for the fill to find, and
     RespecBotForRole could not make one because InitTalentsBySpecNo is a
     no-op with zero talent points. The fallback in FillLfgRaidGroup then
     added bodies of the wrong shape rather than leave the group short.

     The defaults are now tank/heal lines that need no talent points to
     function: warrior protection, paladin protection, druid feral (no Cat
     Form spell yet means bear), shaman restoration, priest holy as before.
     AiFactory's strategy setup keys on the same tab, so behaviour, role
     icon and queue declaration all agree for untalented bots.

  2. FillLfgRaidGroup counted EXISTING group members by that same talent-tab
     guess. A real low-level player who queued as dps was counted as the
     group's tank, suppressing the fill's own tank slot -- the "1 tank and
     4 dps" half of the report even when a capable bot existed. It now
     counts each member's DECLARED LFG role (sLFGMgr->GetRoles, what they
     actually queued as) and only falls back to the guess when no role was
     declared at all.

Applies on top of 0016 (fill shaping) and 0023 (one role definition).

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/Factory/AiFactory.cpp
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/Factory/AiFactory.cpp
--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/Factory/AiFactory.cpp
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/Factory/AiFactory.cpp b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/Factory/AiFactory.cpp
@@ -1,12 +1,32 @@
         uint8 tab = 0;
 
+        // Report #129: an untalented bot used to resolve as the "default" tab
+        // for every role-capable class -- arms warrior, ret paladin, balance
+        // druid, enhance shaman -- so every bot in a level band below the talent
+        // system (and every freshly created one) counted as DPS. The LFD fill
+        // could not find a tank or healer in the band because the band had
+        // none, and 1 tank/4 dps or 5 dps groups were the result. These
+        // defaults are class-appropriate tank/heal lines that need no talent
+        // points to function at low level: AiFactory's strategy setup, the bot's
+        // actual behaviour, and PlayerbotAI::GetDungeonRole (which reads this
+        // same tab) now all agree for untalented bots. Priests already
+        // defaulted to Holy; the pure dps classes keep tab 0.
         switch (bot->getClass())
         {
             case CLASS_MAGE:
                 tab = MAGE_TAB_FROST;
                 break;
+            case CLASS_WARRIOR:
+                tab = WARRIOR_TAB_PROTECTION;
+                break;
             case CLASS_PALADIN:
-                tab = PALADIN_TAB_RETRIBUTION;
+                tab = PALADIN_TAB_PROTECTION;
+                break;
+            case CLASS_DRUID:
+                tab = DRUID_TAB_FERAL;
+                break;
+            case CLASS_SHAMAN:
+                tab = SHAMAN_TAB_RESTORATION;
                 break;
             case CLASS_PRIEST:
                 tab = PRIEST_TAB_HOLY;

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
@@ -1754,8 +1754,15 @@
     uint32 tanks = 0;
     uint32 healers = 0;
     for (GroupReference* itr = group->GetFirstMember(); itr != nullptr; itr = itr->next())
     {
         if (Player* member = itr->GetSource())
         {
-            uint8 const role = LfgFillRoleOf(member);
+            // Report #129: count the role the member DECLARED when it queued
+            // (real players declare through the role check; bots through
+            // LfgJoinAction::GetRoles). GetDungeonRole guesses from the talent
+            // tab, which is wrong for an untalented or casually-specced real
+            // player -- counting one as the group's tank suppressed the fill's
+            // own tank slot. Only fall back to the guess when nobody queued a
+            // role (a manually assembled group mid-fill).
+            uint8 const declared = sLFGMgr->GetRoles(member->GetGUID());
+            uint8 const role = declared & ~lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_LEADER ? declared : LfgFillRoleOf(member);
             if (role == lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_TANK)
                 ++tanks;
             else if (role == lfg::PLAYER_ROLE_HEALER)
